From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:17:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mips: x2600: keep the partly covered lines when invalidating
 a range

invalidate_dcache_range() invalidated every line the range touches. A
line only partly inside it holds other data too, maybe dirty, and that
was lost. Write the first and last lines back first when they are
partial, L1 then L2, as Ingenic's mips_sc_inv() and Linux's
dma_cache_inv() do. Aligned ranges, all U-Boot's DMA buffers until
now, are unchanged.

Needed once the MSC reads by DMA: a file system read can target any
buffer. Checked with reads to buffers 2, 4, 0x20 and 0x3c bytes past a
line start, a dirty word just before each: the word survives.

Signed-off-by: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
---
 arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/cache.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/cache.c b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/cache.c
index 74137ad0..07f55aa9 100644
--- a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/cache.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/cache.c
@@ -77,9 +77,27 @@ void flush_dcache_range(ulong start_addr, ulong stop)
 	sync();
 }
 
+/*
+ * A line only partly inside [start, stop) holds other data too, maybe
+ * dirty: it is written back first, as Ingenic's mips_sc_inv() and Linux's
+ * dma_cache_inv() do, or that data is lost.
+ */
 void invalidate_dcache_range(ulong start_addr, ulong stop)
 {
+	ulong l1 = l1d_line(), l2 = l2_line();
+
+	if (start_addr >= stop)
+		return;
+	if (start_addr & (l1 - 1))
+		mips_cache(HIT_WRITEBACK_INV_D, (void *)(start_addr & ~(l1 - 1)));
+	if (stop & (l1 - 1))
+		mips_cache(HIT_WRITEBACK_INV_D, (void *)(stop & ~(l1 - 1)));
 	l2_hit_war();
+	if (l2 && (start_addr & (l2 - 1)))
+		mips_cache(HIT_WRITEBACK_INV_SD,
+			   (void *)(start_addr & ~(l2 - 1)));
+	if (l2 && (stop & (l2 - 1)))
+		mips_cache(HIT_WRITEBACK_INV_SD, (void *)(stop & ~(l2 - 1)));
 	range(start_addr, stop, l2_line(), HIT_INVALIDATE_SD);
 	range(start_addr, stop, l1d_line(), HIT_INVALIDATE_D);
 	sync();
-- 
